# netsurf: a style attribute change on a sheet the sibling scan gave up on declines only for a + or ~ after [style] (patch 409)
# Generated 2026-11-08
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 408)
#
# The census's "a sibling selector can match on the style attribute" (7:
# wpblog 3, oldreddit, stackoverflow, wpnews, youtube). A debug build
# (scratch only): every one came through html_rl_style_sibling_risk's
# state-2 branch -- a sheet patch 186's scan gave up on (a pseudo-class in
# a sibling rule's left compound), then patch 310's textual scan: "can
# this sheet select on the attribute at all", which also declines on any
# backslash outside a string. oldreddit's, stackoverflow's and youtube's
# sheets have no [style at all -- only escaped class names (.md\:flex,
# Tailwind's .w-\[10px\]); wpblog's and wpnews' [style*=...] selectors sit
# in descendant or :not() positions, which the element's rebuild covers.
#
#  - html_rl_style_sib_scan / html_rl_style_sel_risk: the selectors
#    themselves. Comments, strings and declaration blocks skipped, escapes
#    skipped outside strings, at-rule blocks (@media...) recursed, preludes
#    started past white space and comments. Risk only for a + or ~ after a
#    [style...] selector in the same complex selector; conservatively for a
#    backslash, or a '|' not of '|=', inside [...] (an escape or a
#    namespace could hide the name), @import (imported rules are not in
#    the text), a rule nested in declarations, anything unterminated or
#    nested deeper than 32. (patch 370's reasoning: the rebuild re-selects
#    the element and its subtree; :has() never matches here.)
#  - html_rl_style_sibling_risk: the state-2 branch is a risk only when
#    BOTH patch 310's scan and this one say so -- a sheet with no [style
#    and no backslash cannot select on the attribute, and the selector
#    scan's conservative exits (@import, nesting) must not turn that into a
#    risk (the first version did, on claude: 0 -> 3 declines in the r122
#    A/B). Sheets the 186 scan parsed keep the precise compound check.
#
--- a/content/handlers/html/html.c	2026-11-08 05:36:50.600649445 +0000
+++ b/content/handlers/html/html.c	2026-11-08 06:46:30.982605211 +0000
